        caption="Four frames: the client engineer adjusting a drive at the line, an error caught on the laptop, the hardware check, and customer support." />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="col sec chap" aria-labelledby="c-mobile">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="c-mobile">A mobile version, for work at height</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="body">
      <p>This was our APAC team's first physical product, and since the studio was founded to digitise Eaton's product ecosystem, we tried to make the most of it. The scope was desktop only at first, because the tool depends on USB and a hardware connection. During the design we found scenarios that involve work at height, where a <span class="nb">USB-only</span> connection doesn't serve. After long discussion with my mentor and our design manager, I was entrusted with starting a mobile, <span class="nb">Bluetooth-based</span> solution, with future cloud data integration in mind. In my final days I started it and iterated on it, and left prototypes and detailed documentation for my mentor and the interns who'd follow.</p>
    </div>
